00:32:32,700 --> 00:32:42,340
And there are a few people over 42 in here who are considered to be seen as,

220
00:32:42,340 --> 00:32:45,860
plus the fact that you're 10 years old.

221
00:32:45,860 --> 00:32:48,360
No, no, we have the job of property rights.

222
00:32:48,360 --> 00:32:51,760
Our problem is how do we build it in such a form

223
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:56,620
that we make it compatible with the requirements

224
00:32:56,620 --> 00:32:59,360
of the economy for flexibility

225
00:32:59,360 --> 00:33:02,700
short of drastic catastrophe.

226
00:33:02,700 --> 00:33:04,620
Those are our problems.

227
00:33:04,620 --> 00:33:07,400
To limit property rights, you don't have to worry

228
00:33:07,400 --> 00:33:10,820
about limiting the duration of property rights.

229
00:33:10,820 --> 00:33:14,940
That was something the Roman lawyers were worried about,

230
00:33:14,940 --> 00:33:18,940
But since about 1100, we have known that property rights are very strong.

231
00:33:18,940 --> 00:33:22,660
Don't worry about the intent of property.

232
00:33:22,660 --> 00:34:12,690
The doors are closed and I can be indiscreet.

233
00:34:12,690 --> 00:34:17,690
Schoolmasters have always trained people for jobs that don't exist.

234
00:34:19,980 --> 00:34:25,980
Unfortunately, education doesn't have enough of an impact to corrupt the young.

235
00:34:27,980 --> 00:34:34,470
Most of us have survived our education, haven't you?

236
00:34:34,470 --> 00:34:38,470
Except for those like me who never had any.

237
00:34:38,470 --> 00:34:47,810
No, seriously. All we can do, but it's important, and believe me, it's important, not just humanity.

238
00:34:47,810 --> 00:34:55,260
It's even more important in medicine, and I've been working with medical schools for 40 years,

239
00:34:55,260 --> 00:35:03,260
and what they're doing is totally obsolete, and we know that the rock of the year 2000 will be quite different.

240
00:35:03,260 --> 00:35:09,500
we don't know yet how to train them or help them. All you can do is to build in what the medical

241
00:35:09,500 --> 00:35:18,000
schools do now. The willingness and the ability of the students to learn. We are much better off in

242
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:24,940
management because so many of our students are older. I think that if you ask me what's the

243
00:35:24,940 --> 00:35:33,060
greatest advance in management in the last 40 years, it is that our students by and large are

244
00:35:33,060 --> 00:35:47,650
And so many of them have some experience under their belt and can reflect, project what we tell them, their experience, and so many come back again.

245
00:35:47,650 --> 00:36:03,820
And all of you know that the wealth of management education today does not happen in institutions which pay your salary, but it happens in companies and government offices and so on.

246
00:36:03,820 --> 00:36:10,820
And you do. Most of the work is done by people who are teaching management in our colleges.

247
00:36:10,820 --> 00:36:18,610
But they may teach on campus, but it's a group from the county tax collector's office.

248
00:36:18,610 --> 00:36:22,230
Or they may do it in a corporate office.

249
00:36:22,230 --> 00:36:30,100
And believe me, the justice-affecting edge of education is no longer the teaching of the young,

250
00:36:30,100 --> 00:36:36,380
but the teaching of adults, particularly through management.

251
00:36:36,380 --> 00:36:54,410
And that is to make sure that your students realize that what they learn, the most important is how to learn, how to change, how to reach for new things.

252
00:36:54,410 --> 00:37:24,510
And then preach to friends that the ones who really need what you have to give the most are not 22-year-olds who, by the time they get to where they belong for 10 years later, it's gone.

253
00:37:24,510 --> 00:37:43,060
It's those 35 and 45-year-olds first time now that really are in a job where they need, where they understand, and then I hope they will have acquired the habit of coming back.

254
00:37:43,060 --> 00:37:54,180
I hope that the management is best taught to people who have 10 years of experience.

255
00:37:54,180 --> 00:38:20,670
And fortunately, that's where the center of gravity is shifted, and that, I think, is our great achievement, that we have gotten across, and it's the management people, that the people who, you know, and I went to spitefully to everybody, that when you stop going, those things are cut.

256
00:38:20,670 --> 00:39:00,440
There is almost no thing in between, not yet common, but in this country, that's one of our greatest, and this country has become accepted that professional people, the more they need, the more they want to go back and learn again. And I think that's the greatest strength this country has, and it's a solid achievement for our management. That's what we have to talk about.
